-- Motion preferences: an app-wide animations switch, and one that narrows it
-- to the triage deck's own card animations.
--
-- `animationsEnabled` is the master: everything the app animates deliberately
-- is expected to honour it. `triageDeckAnimations` covers only the swipe
-- deck's fly-out, undo re-entry and stack promotion (ADR 0010), so someone who
-- wants motion everywhere else can still turn off the one screen that throws a
-- card across the display. Readers take the AND of the two.
--
-- Both default to 1, which is exactly how the app behaved before this
-- migration: an existing install upgrades into its current behaviour and
-- nothing changes until the user asks for it.
--
-- Per-device, and deliberately NOT synced — same category as
-- `triageControlScheme`/`triageTutorialSeen` (4.sqm) and
-- `collectionEntry.notificationsMuted` (ADR 0009). How much motion is
-- comfortable is a property of a device and the person holding it, not of the
-- library the account owns.
ALTER TABLE appSettings ADD COLUMN animationsEnabled INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1;
ALTER TABLE appSettings ADD COLUMN triageDeckAnimations INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1;
